From 0003-gmux-i915-switcheroo Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Krzysztof Kowalski <krzysztof7kowalski@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 26 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 0003/0005] platform/x86: apple-gmux: harden discrete GPU
 power-on sequence and detect power-cycle

gmux_set_discrete_state() currently writes the DISCRETE_POWER sequence
(1 -> 3 for ON, 1 -> 0 for OFF), waits at most 200 ms for the GPE
(powerchange_done) and unconditionally returns 0. Two gaps:

1. The power-on is never verified. If the GPE times out or the rail
   sequence fails to latch, the driver proceeds as if the GPU is up,
   and the subsequent client resume fails with a dead card. Read back
   GMUX_PORT_DISCRETE_POWER after the wait: it latches the requested
   value (0x03 = ON, 0x00 = OFF) once the microcontroller has finished
   sequencing the core/VRAM/PCIe rails, so it doubles as a status check.

2. Nothing tells the rest of the stack that the GPU went through a hard
   power-cycle. On the MacBookPro11,3 the gmux cut is deeper than D3cold
   and wipes the VBIOS/PCIe link state; the bound DRM client must reload
   it. Track the previous state and, on an OFF->ON transition, log the
   event. The actual client notification is done by vga_switcheroo right
   after ->power_state() returns (see the vga_switcheroo reinit callback
   patch), because the handler API only knows client IDs, not pci_devs.

Read-only note: on this machine a live test was not performed (writing
the DISCRETE_POWER register is out of scope for the read-only research).

Signed-off-by: Krzysztof Kowalski <krzysztof7kowalski@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/platform/x86/apple-gmux.c | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git i/drivers/platform/x86/apple-gmux.c w/drivers/platform/x86/apple-gmux.c
index 9c728ac4e..d92c435cc 100644
--- i/drivers/platform/x86/apple-gmux.c
+++ w/drivers/platform/x86/apple-gmux.c
@@ -510,6 +510,9 @@ static int gmux_switch_ddc(enum vga_switcheroo_client_id id)
 static int gmux_set_discrete_state(struct apple_gmux_data *gmux_data,
 				   enum vga_switcheroo_state state)
 {
+	enum vga_switcheroo_state old_state = gmux_data->power_state;
+	u8 power;
+
 	reinit_completion(&gmux_data->powerchange_done);

 	if (state == VGA_SWITCHEROO_ON) {
@@ -522,13 +525,42 @@ static int gmux_set_discrete_state(struct apple_gmux_data *gmux_data,
 		pr_debug("Discrete card powered down\n");
 	}

-	gmux_data->power_state = state;
-
+	/*
+	 * Wait for the GPE (powerchange_done) to signal that the gmux
+	 * microcontroller has finished sequencing the core/VRAM/PCIe power
+	 * rails. The timeout is 200 ms, matching the firmware's expected
+	 * power-change latency.
+	 */
 	if (gmux_data->gpe >= 0 &&
 	    !wait_for_completion_interruptible_timeout(&gmux_data->powerchange_done,
 						       msecs_to_jiffies(200)))
 		pr_warn("Timeout waiting for gmux switch to complete\n");

+	/*
+	 * Read back the latched power state. GMUX_PORT_DISCRETE_POWER holds
+	 * the value once the rail sequencing has finished (0x03 = ON,
+	 * 0x00 = OFF), so this doubles as a power status check: it catches a
+	 * GPE that timed out or a rails sequence that failed to latch.
+	 */
+	power = gmux_read8(gmux_data, GMUX_PORT_DISCRETE_POWER);
+	if ((state == VGA_SWITCHEROO_ON && power != 3) ||
+	    (state == VGA_SWITCHEROO_OFF && power != 0))
+		pr_warn("Discrete card power state mismatch: wanted %s, read 0x%02x\n",
+			state == VGA_SWITCHEROO_ON ? "ON" : "OFF", power);
+
+	gmux_data->power_state = state;
+
+	/*
+	 * A hard power-cycle (OFF -> ON) wipes the discrete GPU's firmware
+	 * state (VBIOS, PCIe link training). vga_switcheroo notifies the
+	 * bound client via its ->reinit callback right after our
+	 * ->power_state() handler returns, so the driver can reload the
+	 * VBIOS before resuming. Log the transition here so it is easy to
+	 * correlate in dmesg.
+	 */
+	if (old_state == VGA_SWITCHEROO_OFF && state == VGA_SWITCHEROO_ON)
+		pr_info("Discrete card was power-cycled, client reinit required\n");
+
 	return 0;
 }

